INT. HEARSE, MOVING - NIGHT

Dark road. Rain. The coffin in back is empty of a body. Full of cash.

THANDIWE "TANDI" KOWALCZYK drives. Gloves. Eyes forward.

LAURENCE BECKFORD sits shotgun. Counts. Loses count. Counts again.

In the back, folding the seats down, MIREILLE DUVAL and ISADORE "IZZY" NKEMELU. She tapes a bag. He wipes prints from a crowbar.

She hums. He tells her to stop.

She doesn't.

He rubs his temples. She kicks the coffin lid shut.

LAURENCE
(to the car)
Nobody speak.

IZZY
We're past that.

MIREILLE
We're past everything.

She laughs. He doesn't. He holds the crowbar a moment too long.

TANDI
Eyes on the mirror. Both of you.

They look. Headlights. Far behind. Two white dots, steady.

She slows. He glances back at the dots, then at her. She doesn't speed up.

LAURENCE
Tandi.

TANDI
I see it.

The hearse drifts onto the shoulder. She cuts the engine. Rain on the roof. The headlights grow.

They wait. He puts the crowbar down. She takes her gloves off, one finger at a time.

The car passes. A taxi. It disappears into the rain.

Nobody moves for a long time.

MIREILLE
(softly)
Well. That's the last of the fear.

IZZY
Is it?

She starts the engine.
